From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 02:45:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: vfe: reference count the power domain
 link

vfe_pm_domain_on() and vfe_pm_domain_off() have two independent callers.
vfe_get()/vfe_put() drive them for the VFE the pipeline is streaming on,
and ispif_reset() drives them through camss_pm_domain_on/off() because
the ISPIF reset needs the vfe0, csi_vfe0, vfe1 and csi_vfe1 clocks, all
of which live inside the VFE power domains.

Both users share a single struct device_link pointer with no reference
count. The first off() deletes the link and clears the pointer while the
other user still holds a reference, and the second off() then calls
device_link_del(NULL):

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual
  address 0000000000000324
  pc : device_link_put_kref+0xc/0xa4
  lr : device_link_del+0x2c/0x44
  Call trace:
   device_link_put_kref+0xc/0xa4 (P)
   device_link_del+0x2c/0x44
   vfe_pm_domain_off+0x28/0x3c [qcom_camss]
   vfe_put+0x98/0xbc [qcom_camss]
   vfe_set_power+0x38/0x48 [qcom_camss]
   pipeline_pm_power_one+0xdc/0x104 [videodev]
   v4l2_pipeline_pm_put+0x40/0x80 [videodev]
   video_unprepare_streaming+0x18/0x24 [qcom_camss]
   __vb2_queue_cancel+0x54/0x2b8 [videobuf2_common]
   vb2_ioctl_streamoff+0x5c/0x90 [videobuf2_v4l2]

This fires on every VIDIOC_STREAMOFF, so closing a camera oopses and the
machine reboots. It is reached on any SoC that pairs the ISPIF with a
VFE that has a power domain, which is msm8998, sdm660, msm8996 and
msm8953.

The driver core already handles nesting: device_link_add() on an
existing consumer/supplier pair with DL_FLAG_STATELESS takes another
kref and hands back the same link, and device_link_del() drops one. So
only the driver's own bookkeeping is wrong. Count the users and clear
the cached pointer when the last one goes away, leaving one
device_link_del() per device_link_add() as before.

Fixes: eb73facec2c2 ("media: qcom: camss: Use common VFE pm_domain_on/pm_domain_off where applicable")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c | 8 ++++++--
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
index 3e36cf7e65ed..7a57f0b5fca4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.c
@@ -875,11 +875,13 @@ void vfe_isr_reset_ack(struct vfe_device *vfe)
  */
 void vfe_pm_domain_off(struct vfe_device *vfe)
 {
-	if (!vfe->genpd)
+	if (!vfe->genpd || !vfe->genpd_count)
 		return;
 
 	device_link_del(vfe->genpd_link);
-	vfe->genpd_link = NULL;
+
+	if (!--vfe->genpd_count)
+		vfe->genpd_link = NULL;
 }
 
 /*
@@ -900,6 +902,8 @@ int vfe_pm_domain_on(struct vfe_device *vfe)
 	if (!vfe->genpd_link)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	vfe->genpd_count++;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h
index 64318a64f946..a8f601cdd658 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe.h
@@ -175,6 +175,7 @@ struct vfe_device {
 	struct camss_video_ops video_ops;
 	struct device *genpd;
 	struct device_link *genpd_link;
+	unsigned int genpd_count;
 };
 
 struct camss_subdev_resources;
